{
  "name": "Candle",
  "created": "2026-09-13T18:24:54.210Z",
  "notes": "One small flame and the glow it throws. The flame is a short soft `line` coloured by DENSITY, so its soft edges are red and its core runs to amber -- a candle is hotter in the middle. The halo is a wide, very soft line under it at a fifth the opacity.\n\nThe flicker is a perlin LFO multiplied by the Flicker knob through `M6` (math mul), so the knob sets how much the flame dances rather than how bright it is. A slow `sample_hold` gutters the flame now and then: it dips the brightness a little and, through `M0.rate`, makes the flicker hurry while it recovers, the way a draught catches a real one. A slower perlin sways the flame a hair either side of centre and breathes the halo.",
